POST /documents/{id}/process
          │
          ▼
    Find document
          │
          ├── Not found ──────────► 404
          │
          ▼
         OCR
          │
          ├── No text ────────────► 422
          └── Failure ────────────► 503
          │
          ▼
    Classification
          │
          └── Failure ────────────► 503
          │
          ▼
   Metadata Extraction
          │
          └── Failure ────────────► 503
          │
          ▼
      Save Metadata
          │
          └── DB failure ─────────► 500
          │
          ▼
  Chunking + Embeddings
          │
          └── Failure ────────────► 503
          │
          ▼
       Response

What we should do now

We should implement/verify the error handling in this exact process flow before moving to anything else.

The important distinction is:

/process
    ↓
OCR → Classification → Metadata → Save → Chunks/Embeddings

while:

/summarize
    ↓
OCR + Stored Metadata → LLM → Summary

and:

/search
    ↓
Embedding → pgvector → Relevant Chunks

So yes, /process absolutely needs to be handled.




Final processing architecture
POST /documents/{id}/process
          │
          ▼
    Find document
          │
          ├── Not found ──────────► 404
          │
          ▼
         OCR
          │
          ├── No text ────────────► 422
          └── Failure ────────────► 503
          │
          ▼
    Classification
          │
          └── Failure ────────────► 503
          │
          ▼
   Metadata Extraction
          │
          └── Failure ────────────► 503
          │
          ▼
      Save Metadata
          │
          └── DB failure ─────────► 500
          │
          ▼
  Chunking + Embeddings
          │
          └── Failure ────────────► 503
          │
          ▼
       Response
Summary
POST /documents/{id}/summarize
          │
          ▼
    Find document
          │
          ▼
         OCR
          │
          ▼
   Stored Metadata
          │
          └──────┐
                 ▼
                LLM
